IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wcima-compensation`
IMPORT `wcima-qa`

-- Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act 2023 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (wcima-qa.l4): every exported
-- question, for every role and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the answer
-- must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error. Each
-- question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with FALSE (the situation does not hold) and every
-- later input ASSUMEd: the answer must be `does not arise for you`. Every situation input is a BOOLEAN, and the helpers
-- that read the one enumeration the employer's claim questions take list every value with no OTHERWISE, so the trap of
-- graffiti finding 31 cannot hide a read.
--
-- For the worker (the baseline's seat), each case is asserted twice: once against a value worked by hand from the text
-- (most taken from the baseline's own cases, wcima-cases-compensation.l4, and its lives k044, k085, d044, d080), and
-- once against the baseline export's own answer on the same facts, carried into the layer's answer type. For the
-- employer the values are worked by hand from the text. Day counts take the day of the claim, or of receipt, as day 0.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked date` IS A DATE
ASSUME `an unasked engagement` IS A `My engagement`
ASSUME `an unasked class` IS A `Prescribed class`
ASSUME `an unasked assessor` IS AN Assessor
ASSUME `an unasked requester` IS A `Who requested the assessment`
ASSUME `an unasked item` IS A `Table item`
ASSUME `an unasked defendant` IS A Defendant
ASSUME `an unasked insurance` IS A `How I am insured`

`as the worker` MEANS `I was injured at work, or in work I do for someone`
`as the employer` MEANS `I employ someone who was injured at work, or contracted their employer for the work`

-- The engagements of the baseline's cases (wcima-cases-compensation.l4), restated here: a case file is not imported.
`Jake's delivery riding on an ABN, April 2029` MEANS `My engagement` WITH
    `I have a contract of service` IS FALSE
    `I am an apprentice under a contract and a registered training contract` IS FALSE
    `I contracted to do the work myself` IS TRUE
    `the work is part of a trade or business I regularly carry on in my own or a business name` IS TRUE
    `I sublet the contract` IS FALSE
    `I employ a worker` IS FALSE
    `I do part of the work personally` IS FALSE

`the same riding, if it were not his own business` MEANS `My engagement` WITH
    `I have a contract of service` IS FALSE
    `I am an apprentice under a contract and a registered training contract` IS FALSE
    `I contracted to do the work myself` IS TRUE
    `the work is part of a trade or business I regularly carry on in my own or a business name` IS FALSE
    `I sublet the contract` IS FALSE
    `I employ a worker` IS FALSE
    `I do part of the work personally` IS FALSE

`a contractor who employs a rider and rides none of the work himself` MEANS `My engagement` WITH
